ACCRETING LIFE IN ANOTHER WORLD FROM ZERO

A dream, I had a dream.

A dream that would not fade, a dream that kept repeating, a dream with no end, a dream that would not end――.

Over and over again, many many times over, repeating mistakes over and over, correcting them more and more. 

One thousand times, spinning. Ten thousand times, connecting. One hundred million times, overcoming them. 

And before knowing it, losing track of counting.

Agony, terror, turbidity, ruin, hatred, madness. 

Exhausted, shaken, twisted, corrupted, contorted, decayed, anguished; a heart smashed to pieces.

And yet, there was still a place I wanted to reach. 

And yet, there was still a wish I wanted to protect.

Even if no one knew about the endless tragedies that repeated over and over, I would not forget.

Even if no one notices, only I am unable to forget.

――Even if the people I want to save wept, I still want to save them.

So, even now, I do not regret having taken that hand.

If there is something I regret, it would be that I was hesitant and indecisive in taking her hand, and the frustration towards my own weak, fragile heart that I could not steel.

