Subaru frowned and sighed at the report that had come from Elsa, who licked her blood-red lips.

Once again, it was a miss. Subaru’s arrow had missed its target, and the target had gotten away again.

In search of the whereabouts of the Sin Archbishop of Gluttony, he had set up an information network in various locations, hunting down every Witch Cultist from one end to the other; yet, Gluttony was nowhere to be found.

Subaru: [In the end, the only one we’ve killed is Greed.]

Elsa: [That, and Wrath was captured. I think that was a success, but I guess it might not be for you.]

Subaru: […Anyway, I got your report. For now, remain on standby until I need you again. If there’s anything I need to ask of you, I’ll contact you again.]

Elsa: [Yes. Understood. By the way, I’d like to meet with Meili…]

Subaru: [――You can’t. But, I won’t hold her captive forever. At most, you’ll need to be patient until the Royal Selection is settled.]

Rejecting Elsa’s request, Subaru emphasized the duration of their agreement. In response, Elsa replied with a brief “Yes, I understand”, and headed straight for the window rather than the door.

Since Subaru’s room was on the third floor of the mansion, she had probably entered through that window. It was not surprising that she managed to pull off such a feat of acrobatics――,

Subaru: [Ah, wait, Elsa. There’s one more thing I want you to ask you.]

Elsa: [――? What may that be? I don’t really know anything of much importance.]

Subaru: [It’s nothing that important. Since you came from outside… how was the weather beyond the forest? Was it raining or anything?]

Elsa: [The weather? Ah, there was no problem with it whatsoever. The clouds are a bit thick, but there’s no need to worry about it getting worse. Is that all?]

Subaru: [No…]

Twisting his head to the side, Subaru gazed at the Magic Time Crystal in his room. Right now, it was already Fire Time―― it had gone past seven Bright Time, and was now just after lunchtime.

After confirming this, Subaru walked over to Elsa, her feet still planted on the windowsill,

Subaru: [I want to ask you to do something. ――Please, cut off my head with that knife.]

Elsa: [――Your head… I wonder, have you lost it already?]

Subaru: [I’m being completely sane, okay? I’m just asking you to do something that has to be done.]

Curiously widening her eyes at Subaru’s remarks, Elsa emanated a fierce aura. But, Subaru’s attitude remained unflinching.

Seeing his imposing manner, Elsa shrugged her shoulders.

Elsa: [Generally speaking, most people who have their heads cut off usually die.]

Subaru: [I suppose I also fall under that category. I’m not sure about you, though.]

Elsa: [I think I too would die if my head were to come off… Are you sure about this?]

Subaru: [Don’t worry, this won’t cause any harm to Meili. I’ll have someone bring you written instructions later so you’ll know where Meili is. Is that okay?]

As Subaru assuaged her concerns with his reassuring words, Elsa contemplated for a moment. However, after only a few seconds of thought, she slowly unsheathed her weapon――,

Elsa: [Do you have any last words?]

Subaru: [Make it painless.]

Elsa: [――――]

Subaru: [Ah. I told you about Meili, but you can do whatever you want with my guts after I’m dead. Just don’t lay a finger on anyone in the mansion. Well, I guess that’s why I have Reinhard arou――]

Before he could finish saying those words, Elsa’s arm sliced through the air.

For just a moment, Subaru’s field of vision was turned upside down. As his view of the room spun around, he watched as blood splattered all over that familiar room, and,

――Ah, cleaning this room is going to be hard on Petra.

And, with that thought, Subaru’s life blinked out.

△▼△▼△▼△

――When he woke up from his hollow dreams, Subaru always experienced a suffocating sensation.

However, this time, his release from there was much quicker.

Perhaps, it was because Natsuki Subaru was being reconstructed in a manner different from him waking from sleep.

Subaru: [――――]

Subaru jerked up violently, placing his hand against his sweat-drenched forehead. It was cooler than the perspiration typical of sleep, closer to the cold sweat that flowed when faced with the shock of losing his life.

In any case, Subaru’s body was atop the sofa in his own room, and sunlight was streaming in through the window.

Subaru: […Morning, huh?]

Touching his neck which should have been cut, Subaru rose slowly. Cocking his head, making sure that his head had not fallen to the floor inadvertently, he checked the time using the Magical Time Crystal above his door.

The Crystal was glowing a pale green, indicating that it was currently early morning.

Then, the question that remained was “which” morning it was――.

Subaru: [――――]

To confirm this, Subaru quickly pulled out the Magic Crystal around his neck.

As he clutched the ticket that connected this dream world with reality, the tapping of this foot, as if he were in a rush, overlapped with hot pulses, and Subaru’s consciousness was engulfed by a white light.

Subaru: [――――]

When he opened his eyes, Subaru was once again standing in the middle of the vast grassy plain.

Turning around, he saw a hill, and under a parasol atop that hill, a Witch clad in black faced a white table, gracefully sipping from her cup.

Ascending the hill, he headed towards the Witch.

Subaru: [Hey, what day…]

Echidna: [――――]

Placing his hands on the table, he snarled at the Witch who continued her elegant tea-time. However, she replied not, and simply pointed silently at the seat across from her.

The seat was empty, and a cup of tea had been prepared for a visitor. What she had presented to Subaru was the minimum requirement for participating in her tea party――.

Subaru: [Damn it, I guess I should just drink it, I’ll drink it!]

Grabbing the cup whilst clicking his tongue, Subaru gulped down all of the cup’s contents in one swig. Instantly, the heat of the freshly brewed tea burned his throat.

Subaru: [Ghhhuaa――!?]

Echidna: [Whoaa!? Just a second, just a second! You do know that there was really no need for that?]

Subaru: [Shut up! You play the part of a difficult to please Witch, and this only happened because you insist on making me follow such complicated procedures… ghha, ghhk gh!]

As Subaru choked on the tea he had swallowed, even Echidna hurriedly stood up from her seat. She then placed her hand on Subaru’s back, and continued to rub his back until his coughing subsided.

Then, after a moment of Subaru’s sputtering,

Subaru: [Ghha, ack… ah, I’ve calmed down… eh, what about the tea?]

Echidna: [Ah, it is fine this time. Also, there is no fun in having you spit out the tea that I worked so hard to brew. And, the table too, it would be a pity to leave it stained like this.]

Echidna shook her head as Subaru, wiping his mouth, tried to correct his transgression.

Then, with a snap of her fingers, the table that was sullied with the tea Subaru had spit out dissipated, quickly transforming the scene under the parasol into a desolate landscape.

Echidna: [Come now, you even dirtied the chair a bit. Making me stand here to talk to you, what  a very sinful man you are.]

Subaru: [I was just choking on my tea and spat out. ――Compared to that, we have more important things to discuss.]

Cutting off the teasing words of Echidna, Subaru raised his finger.

That which he had to confirm, was only one thing.

Subaru: [What day is it today? What’s the month and date?]

Echidna: [――Hmm. From that question, I assume you have returned again?]

Subaru: [Yeah. Yes, that’s right. I just want to be sure of the date. What is it?]

While holding out his Magic Crystal, Subaru asked this of Echidna, who fully understood the situation. Receiving the Magic Crystal, Echidna nodded before beginning to share in his Memories.

Echidna: [The month is Kisdam, the date is the fourteenth.]

Subaru: [――――]

Echidna: [Judging by your expression, it would appear you are half excited and half bewildered.]

Upon seeing Subaru’s reaction, Echidna closed one eye curiously. Subaru nodded with a “Yeah” at her question, his eyes half excited and half bewildered.

Returning to the morning of the day he had Returned by Death was something he had desired. However, it also hinted at the possibility of other anxieties――,

Echidna: [Myon myon myon myon myon…]

Pressing the proffered Magic Crystal against her forehead, Echidna began her goofy inheritance of Memories.

While witnessing this Witch’s ritual, Subaru righted the chair he had overturned, and sat down heavily.

He had some concerns. However, being able to return to this very morning was fortunate. Since the events that had transpired were still fresh in his memory, it would not have been too difficult to positively correct the situation.

Subaru: [There shouldn’t be a problem with Petra, but during morning practice I told Reinhard and Garfiel some unnecessary things. I’ll be more careful with that. Also, if I get scratched by Beatrice, it’ll upset Emilia. But, Beatrice hasn’t spoken to me in a while, so…]

He wanted to visit the Forbidden Library and exchange words with Beatrice as much as possible.

Even if that exchange would be a painful rejection of Subaru in a sorrowful, tearful voice.

Subaru: [Roswaal is the same as usual, and Ram too… ah, she’s going to bring up Frederica in regards to Annerose’s letter, so I gotta come up with a clever response. Also, with Emilia――]

He had to tread carefully, as Emilia could easily go out of control if she saw Subaru’s wounds. However, if he were to deal with the situation in Beatrice’s room from before, Emilia would no longer go berserk.

Yet, he did not want to miss the opportunity to talk to Beatrice. Even if he got scratched, would Emilia remain calm so long as he hid his wounds?

Subaru: [Emilia, Emilia, Emilia…]

Were there any oversights, any mistakes, any irreversible problems?

Reflecting on his half of a day, recalling, recalling, recalling――,

Echidna: [――Natsuki Subaru.]

As Subaru began to overheat in thought, without him noticing, Echidna, standing by his side, touched his cheek.

It appeared that the inheritance of Memories had completed. Echidna gently placed the Magic Crystal back around Subaru’s neck as his eyes widened,

Echidna: [If there is anything you wish to talk about, I shall listen to anything.]

And, that was all she said.

Subaru: [――――]

Hearing those words, Subaru took a short breath and squeezed his eyes tightly shut.

In that quietness, he could feel his feverish thoughts start to calm down. He was okay now; he was fine. It was true that he was so distressed that he felt as if his heart might crack and shatter.

Subaru: [I can handle this much on my own… Thank you.]

Echidna: [――. How surprising. For you to thank me so honestly, you must have been feeling very weak-hearted.]

Raising her eyebrow, Echidna’s words caught Subaru off guard.

He wanted to correct letting those words of gratitude reflexively slip out as some kind of mistake, but the spontaneity made it seem all the more genuine, making it impossible to remedy.

This sensation was something that Subaru had feared. It was something he did not want to put into words.

――He felt more at ease in the dream world with Echidna, than he did in reality where Emilia and his friends were awaiting him.

But such a thing should absolutely not be allowed to happen.

Subaru: [――――]

Echidna: [Well, that is fine. Just seeing that expression on your face is enough of a reward for me.]

Gazing at Subaru, who was silently attempting to cover things up, Echidna said this with a teasing tone.

It was extremely uncomfortable, as if she could see right through him, but the more Subaru pursued the matter, the more disadvantageous it would be for him. So, Subaru did not press the issue any further.

More importantly――,

Subaru: [If you’ve inherited my Memories, then you should understand. The save point has moved. That means…]

Echidna: [――Another problem that threatens your life is fast approaching.]

Echidna was quick to grasp the situation, and Subaru nodded with a tense expression.

The checkpoint for Return by Death always updated when Subaru was in danger. If Return by Death had reset him to this morning, then a life-threatening situation would arise shortly.

Once again, if Death were to befall Natsuki Subaru――,

Subaru: [I’m going to have to borrow your strength again.]

Echidna: [Well, that is what our Contract is all about… Nevertheless, there is just one thing…]

Subaru: [What is it?]

Catching on to her hesitant words, Subaru prompted Echidna to continue. Then, while Echidna twirled her fingers in her long, white hair,

Echidna: [Perhaps I am mistaken, but… you seem to be having a little bit of fun, are you not?]

Subaru: [――. Don’t say such stupid things.]

Subaru snorted in response to her outrageously ridiculous statement.

It was ridiculous, a truly ridiculous thing to say. There was no way something so stupid could be true.

To think that he would find more comfort with the spiral of Death engulfing him, repeating trial and error to escape from it, than he would in peaceful and ordinary days spent with Emilia and his friends.

Subaru: [At best, I’ll be counting on you, Witch of Greed.]

Echidna: [And you, for the sake of satisfying my boundless curiosity, please do your best.]

Ignoring the budding turmoil in his heart, Subaru was ready to take on Echidna and the challenge ahead.

Perhaps it could be said that he had an opportunity for a preemptive strike due to the unexpected update of Return by Death’s checkpoint.

Subaru: [If I were to use Return by Death to make the first strike, could it be useful for a surprise attack?]

Echidna: [It is a rather rare opportunity. I certainly hope to make good use of it. ――Oh, and…]

Subaru: [Yeah?]

Calling out to Subaru as he was about to go off to battle, Echidna pointed to the Magic Crystal hanging around his neck.

Echidna: [Even after reading your memories, I still cannot understand: why did you Return by Death?]

Subaru: [Ah, that. That was because――]

The answer was――,

△▼△▼△▼△

Passing through the door of the dream world, Natsuki Subaru’s consciousness returned to reality.

Subaru: [――――]

Looking above the door of his room, the time shown by the Magical Time Crystal remained the same as it was before. As usual, feeling uncomfortable about the difference between the time he had perceived and time in reality, Subaru headed towards the bathroom.

He washed his face, brushed his teeth, practiced smiling, and quickly changed his clothes.

And, just as he had finished――,

???: [Subaru-sama, are you awake―― wah?]

Subaru: [Hey, good morning, Petra. You’re looking cute this morning, too.]

The door opened abruptly, and Petra stood there on the other side, her eyes wide open. But, after quickly realizing that Subaru was just teasing her, she smiled shyly.

Petra: [Jeez, please don’t surprise me like that.]

Subaru: [I’m sorry, I’m sorry. Well, Petra. Aren’t you going to greet me?]

Petra: [Really, you don’t regret what you did even a little? Hmph… yes, good morning, Subaru-sama. Today is once again a splendid morning, you know.]

Without mentioning Subaru’s frivolous attitude, Petra continued with a lovely smile. Her words were exactly the same as that morning before he had Returned by Death.

That being so, the next thing she would say would be exactly the same.

Subaru: [I agree, it’s indeed a splendid morning. Petra is cute today, too; I don’t even need to say it.]

Petra: [Subaru-sama’s still saying such things.… Ah, but there are clouds hanging over the sky beyond the forest, and it seems that the weather may get worse this afternoon. I have plans to go shopping this afternoon, so I hope it’ll stay sunnyyy.]

He listened to the girl talk about what she wanted to do, speaking in a manner which befitted her age; Subaru let out a laugh. Seeing this, Petra puffed out her cheeks, but he hastily replied with a “I’m sorry, I’m sorry” and continued to speak――,

Subaru: [But, rest assured, Petra. Today will stay sunny all day. The clouds are giving off a false impression and won’t be a problem. I can say that confidently.]

Petra: [Huh? Really? That’s super helpful… But, how do you know that?]

Subaru: [Well, that’s because…]

Petra inclined her head and widened her eyes at Subaru’s assertion.

Giving her a smile that showed his teeth, Subaru answered the girl’s query.

Subaru: [――Because I returned just for this, putting my life on the line for it.]

△▼△▼△▼△

――A plain of green, a small hill, a white-haired Witch in a mournful black dress sitting at a white table under a parasol, gracefully tilting her cup.

Echidna: [Using one’s own life, to save, to protect, to prevent others from being hurt. How great a feat it is to do so not just once, or twice, but repeatedly.]

Letting out an exhilarated sigh, the Witch recalled the image of a boy with whom she was Contracted.

Desperately pursuing his ideals, pressing onward despite being struck endlessly by reality, possessing the most wretched Authority of Return by Death as his own, a lovable human who continued to fight with all of his might. [3]

Echidna: [――But that Authority is a double-edged sword. Too little regard for one’s own life, and one becomes too fixated on the value of lives other than their own. Sacrificing one’s own life, desperately trying to protect the lives of those precious to them… over time, they cannot focus on anything “except” for the lives of those loved ones. That is…]

No matter when, no matter where, that singular attitude of clinging onto one thing was downright foolish.

And, to be foolish, to be ignorant, to be knowable.

Echidna: [――You truly are, someone desirable to me.]

Cheeks reddening like a maiden in the throes of infatuation, the Witch longed for the absent boy.

Through the Magic Crystal connected to his Gate, she felt the boy’s world as if it were her own.

Was he aware of his own dependence on the Witch? He was willing to Return by Death simply to check the weather, unaware of such a mentality.

Echidna: [But, please rest assured. The lives of those whom you treasure, I will wholeheartedly protect them. I will support you with all of my wisdom. So, for this reason, you too――]

――To satisfy this Witch’s inexhaustible curiosity, I want you to continue being my accomplice.

Times of hardship and unreasonable fate would continue to befall this boy endlessly.

No matter how arduous the hardships, how insurmountable the heights, the boy and the Witch would overcome, lending one other strength and wisdom, hand in hand.

Offered by the Witch of Greed was that love of scorching flame. [3]

Echidna: [Ah, even so――]

Feeling the pain in the hearts of the people the boy scrambled to protect, pain that resulted from being protected by that boy, through the boy’s Gate, the Witch sighed.

A proposition that would remain sempiternally unsolved, even in death; an enigma that would eternally enthrall her.

Ah, even so――,

Echidna: [――Why must love fade?]

※　※　※　※　※　※　※　※　※　※　※　※
Epilogue

Echidna: [Myon myon myon myon myon…]

Subaru: [――. I’ve been thinking about this for a while now.]

Echidna: [Yes? What is it? If something is on your mind, feel free to speak. We are in this together, no? Why would you become shy about it now??]

Subaru: [Don’t phrase it in a way that grates my nerves every time… What is this “Myon myon” thing?]

Echidna: [――? Nothing at all, it is merely a ritual for reading your memories from the Magic Crystal.]

Subaru: [Not that, I’m talking about that lackluster chant. Why “Myon myon myon”?]

Echidna: [Oh, that. It would seem that, before I was born, there was a magic user who made quite the name for herself in an era when magic had yet to be systematized.]

Subaru: [Oh, really? Someone like that… are they related to this?]

Echidna: [Yes. The name of that person is Myonmyon.]

Subaru: [Myonmyon!! That was a person’s name!!!!]

Echidna: [So, when those who received her instruction would use magic, they would chant this to remember the words of their master…]

Subaru: [So, you mean that Myonmyon was the master’s name?]

Echidna: [That is how it is. I suppose that mystery has been solved?]

Subaru: [Now that I’ve solved it, I guess it was a mystery I didn’t really need to be bothered with…]

Echidna: [Hey now, you have me explain it to you, and now you say this? What a terrible boy you are.]

Subaru: [And you, who continually accompanies this terrible boy, also have a strange taste.]

Echidna: [Hehe… well, what do you think? Do you regret it?]

Subaru: [Regret what?]

Echidna: [That day, the day in which you took my hand. That is how you have gotten to where you are now.]

Subaru: [――No, I don’t regret it. This, was the best choice I could have made.]

Echidna: […Huh?]

Subaru: [Don’t be such a pushover, Echidna. You and I are in this together. No matter how many times, how many dozens, how many hundreds of times it takes to redo, I’m taking everyone with me into the future. You’re gonna have to tag along for the ride, too.]

Echidna: [My my, I had nearly forgotten. You have quite the talent for flirting with Witches, no?]

Subaru: [It’s not a good idea to start a rumor mill… Hey, you’re not gonna continue with “Myon myon”?]

Echidna: [That is correct. For the time being, I would rather talk to the you of the present than delve into the you of the past.]

Subaru: […I see. Do as you please. Wicked Witch.]

Echidna: [Oh, but of course. ――I, am quite the Wicked Witch, am I not?]

《End》

Translation Notes:

[1] Anchor (依り代, Yorishiro) A vessel for a spirit. As a different example, the crystal Emilia keeps on herself and where Puck rest in an Anchor. Read more.

[2] The idiom in the original Japanese, 「鬼の首を取ったように」is translated literally here as “like taking the head of an oni”. This idiom means to treat something as a big deal when it is not. So Echidna is making a big fuss out of nothing.

[3] In the last section of the chapter, there are two words rendered in katakana rather than kanji, which we decided to italicize. However, it is worth giving a brief explanation of the possible significance of this choice. The two words were human, referring to Subaru, and love, referring to the emotions of Echidna towards Subaru. Often, rendering a word in katakana instead of kanji can be used as a stylistic choice to signify a lack of understanding of the word or an abstraction. My personal belief as a translator is that this is being used to signify that despite the use of these words to describe Subaru as human and Echidna’s love, they are void of the typical meaning we ascribe to these words. They are being wrapped in the common, palatable ideas we are used to, yet are completely antithetical to them. Echidna’s love and Subaru’s humanity are so far off from the concepts of love and humanity we all share, that they are completely different concepts being referred to with the same words. This is backed up by a line in Chapter 1 of Kasaneru: “Even if he were to take the hand of the Witch, he would not lose the soul and dignity of being ‘human’.” The “human” in this line is the same word, but rendered in kanji and with double quotes:『人間』. The transition to this same word now being in katakana shows that taking Echidna’s hand did lead to him losing his humanity.

